# Maven extensions
/.mvn/extensions.xml
# Node.js service (server/)

# Every .env-named variant, not only the two names the service reads: the
# character classes cover case variants (.ENV) because git matches these
# patterns case-sensitively, and the trailing wildcard covers the suffixed
# conventions (.env.local, .env.production) an operator creates beside .env.
.[Ee][Nn][Vv]*
# ...except the committed template, re-included after the rule it overrides
# because a negation only applies to a preceding rule, and path-qualified so
# no other .env.example is re-included. A further committed template needs
# its own negation line here.
!server/.env.example
server/logs/
!server/package-lock.json
